{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Every firstborn.</b> They placed it here because above it dealt with the law of the Hebrew slave, and here <b>you shall not work your firstborn ox</b>; and this passage of the firstborn is repeated here to teach therein the law of the firstborn with a blemish." "<b>That is born.</b> This excludes the one born through the abdominal wall." "<b>The male you shall sanctify.</b> Apply to it the law of sanctity — how so? <b>You shall not work</b> it <b>and you shall not shear</b> it, for it is not yours but to eat it before HaShem, after the throwing of its blood and the burning of its portions; and it does not require libations, nor leaning, nor waving, whether alive or slaughtered."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:52:57.952043475Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}